        "text": "Querying the details of a package\nThe rpm command can be used to query the details of a package installed on the system. For example,\nto query the details of the ftp package, use the following command:\nFormat and Disk Space Commands\n78\nFigure 4.16 \u2013 Querying the details of a package that\u2019s been installed\nThe dpkg and rpm tools are essential for managing software packages and optimizing the use of disk\nspace in Linux and Unix systems. By providing valuable information about package space, dependencies,\nand upgrade options, these tools enable administrators to make informed decisions and ensure the\nstability, security, and performance of the system.",
